  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "<img src=\"https://images.code.org/771ed8cca3da41f35755bddd52002609-image-1682524895513.png\" style=\"width:100px; float:right; margin:0px 0px 0px 20px;\">\r\n\r\n# Resources in Web Lab\r\n\r\nWeb Lab provides several resources for students to explore and become self-sufficient while working through the curriculum.\r\n\r\n# Do This:\r\n\r\n* Click the \"Help and Tips\" dropdown below and explore and resources available to students\r\n* While in one of the resource guides, check out the FAQ section, which has additional tips for students.\r\n   * _Note: As students progress through the unit, they are provided more resource guides - those related to concepts in previous lessons as well as current lesson concepts. All of the guides students will eventually have access to can be found in the menu on the left when in a resource guide (pictured on the right)._ \r\n* Click the Documentation button in the upper-right corner of the instructions pane to see Web Lab's documentation\r\n* When you are finished exploring, continue to the next level\r\n\r\n![]()\r\n\r\n::: details [**Help and Tips**]\r\n- [<i class=\"fa-regular fa-map\"></i> Headings and Paragraphs](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/csd-2024/guides/headings-and-paragraphs)\r\n- [<i class=\"fa-solid fa-book\"></i> HTML Tags](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/csd-2024/guides/html-tags)\r\n:::",
